  "question": {
    "text": "A solid metallic cube having total surface area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is uniformly heated. If its temperature is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, calculate the increase in volume of the cube. (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>&#8728;</mo></mmultiscripts><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)."
  },
